<urn:atm:triage:finding/RUSQLITE-CORE-COUPLING-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RUSQLITE-CORE-COUPLING-001" ;
  triage:title "atm-storage-rusqlite depends on atm-core, violating the backend/storage boundary reset" ;
  triage:description "On integrate/phase-AD @ 51a8b82e, the SQLite backend now has a real normal dependency on atm-core and uses atm-core types/helpers from production code. This contradicts ADR-018's forbidden graph edge atm-storage-* -> atm-core and its mechanical-enforcement rule that backend crates must not depend on atm-core. The coupling currently has two causes: (1) the AD.21 nudge override contract was introduced under atm_core::boundary, forcing atm-storage-rusqlite to implement and return atm-core-owned traits/types; and (2) mailbox metadata reconstruction in atm-storage-rusqlite now imports atm_core::schema::InboxMessage plus atm_core::derive_ack_requirement instead of staying on the canonical atm-storage schema/contracts or a backend-local helper. The issue is not that InboxMessage moved; the canonical definition still lives in atm-storage and atm-core only re-exports it. The violation is that the backend reaches upward into the atm-core facade and business helper layer." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AD" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "ARCH" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crate" ;
  triage:status "closed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-07-11T01:20:17Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:resolutionNote "Implemented on fix/phase-AD-pm-boundary-violation by moving the storage-neutral nudge-template override contract family plus the durable ack-requirement classifier into atm-storage, adding an atm-storage-owned sealed seam, keeping atm-core as a compatibility re-export plus PostSendHookEvent-specific helper only, removing the normal atm-storage-rusqlite -> atm-core Cargo edge, relocating the canonical machine-readable boundary record to boundaries/atm-storage/nudge-template-override-store.toml with ADR-024 superseding ADR-021, and deleting stale atm-storage-rusqlite allowed-dependent entries from atm-core boundary records so boundary lint matches the new graph." ;
  triage:rationale "Validation on this branch passed through the real repo closure lanes: cargo test -p atm-storage, cargo test -p atm-storage-rusqlite, cargo test -p agent-team-mail-core, cargo test --workspace --quiet, python3 .just/lint_boundaries.py, just lint, and just test. Child occurrences remain the original first-observed integrate/phase-AD evidence rather than being rewritten to the fix branch snapshot." ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-10T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RUSQLITE-CORE-COUPLING-001/integrate-AD/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RUSQLITE-CORE-COUPLING-001/integrate-AD/2> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RUSQLITE-CORE-COUPLING-001/integrate-AD/3> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RUSQLITE-CORE-COUPLING-001/integrate-AD/4> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RUSQLITE-CORE-COUPLING-001/integrate-AD/5> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RUSQLITE-CORE-COUPLING-001/integrate-AD/6> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RUSQLITE-CORE-COUPLING-001/integrate-AD/7> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RUSQLITE-CORE-COUPLING-001/integrate-AD/8> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RUSQLITE-CORE-COUPLING-001/integrate-AD/9> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RUSQLITE-CORE-COUPLING-001/integrate-AD/10> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/integrate-AD/51a8b82e> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/integrate-AD/51a8b82e> ;
  triage:notes """Documented during the post-phase-AD boundary investigation.

Required type moves:
1. Move the nudge override storage contract itself off `atm_core::boundary` and into a backend-neutral shared crate surface, most likely `atm-storage`. The moved contract must include `NudgeTemplateOverrideStore`, `BuiltInNudgeTemplateKind`, `TeamNudgeTemplateOverrideMode`, and `TeamNudgeTemplateOverrideRow`.
2. Move the sealing seam with that trait. `atm-storage-rusqlite` must stop implementing `atm_core::boundary::sealed::Sealed`; after the move it should implement an `atm-storage`-owned sealed trait for the override-store boundary instead.
3. Split `BuiltInNudgeTemplateKind` ownership carefully to avoid both a reintroduced forbidden edge and Rust orphan-rule trouble. Move only the storage-neutral enum plus `as_str` / `Display` / `FromStr` logic into `atm-storage`. Do not move `BuiltInNudgeTemplateKind::from_post_send_event(&PostSendHookEvent)` with that enum, because `PostSendHookEvent` remains `atm-core` owned. Replace that method with an `atm-core` owned helper or extension path such as `built_in_nudge_template_kind_from_post_send_event(event: &PostSendHookEvent) -> BuiltInNudgeTemplateKind`, or another core-local wrapper that preserves call-site ergonomics without requiring an `atm-storage -> atm-core` edge or an impl in the wrong crate.
4. Do not move `ResolvedBuiltInNudgeTemplate`, `InternalNudgeEnvelope`, or the rendering helpers. Those are core-side send/nudge execution types and can stay in `atm-core`; they should import the moved `BuiltInNudgeTemplateKind` and `TeamNudgeTemplateOverrideRow` from the new shared contract home.
5. Keep `atm-core`'s boundary facade re-exporting the moved nudge override contract/types during the cutover so downstream consumer crates (`atm-runtime`, `atm-daemon-bootstrap`, and the `atm` internal-nudge tests) do not break while the ownership relocation lands. The cutover plan is: move canonical ownership to `atm-storage`, keep compatibility re-exports in `atm-core::boundary`, then retire those re-exports only after all consumers have moved and the updated boundary record/ADR path is accepted.

Required boundary-record and ADR reconciliation:
1. `boundaries/atm-core/nudge-template-override-store.toml` currently declares `owner_package = "atm-core"` under ADR-021's enforcement path. The implementation plan must explicitly relocate that owner record to the new canonical home or otherwise supersede it with a team-lead-approved replacement boundary record.
2. Update the paired human-readable boundary record in `docs/atm-core/boundaries.md:179-207` so it no longer claims `atm-core` owns the override-store contract once the canonical contract moves.
3. Because ADR-021 specifically governs the accepted dependent widening for this contract, closure requires either:
   - a team-lead ruling that ADR-021 is superseded for this ownership relocation and the new boundary record is the accepted replacement, or
   - a replacement/superseding ADR documenting the move of `NudgeTemplateOverrideStore` ownership out of `atm-core`.
4. The closure condition is not met by code motion alone; the boundary record and ADR/governance update must be complete in the same fix family.

Required mailbox-metadata untangling:
1. Remove `atm-storage-rusqlite/src/mailbox_metadata.rs` imports of `atm_core::derive_ack_requirement`, `atm_core::schema::InboxMessage`, and `atm_core::types::AckRequirementState`.
2. Resolve the design choice firmly: prefer moving the minimal backend-neutral ack-intent classifier/state shape into `atm-storage`, not a backend-local duplicate. This path removes the current `atm-storage-rusqlite -> atm-core` edge while avoiding duplicated ack-state logic across `atm-storage-rusqlite`, `atm-runtime`, and `atm-core`.
3. The minimal shared move must cover the actual current consumer surface, not just mailbox metadata. `AckRequirementState` and the classifier are also consumed by `crates/atm-core/src/read/state.rs`, `crates/atm-core/src/list.rs`, `crates/atm-core/src/service_runtime_store.rs`, and `crates/atm-runtime/src/legacy_storage_adapters.rs`. The plan must treat those as part of the blast radius for the preferred path.
4. Correct the rationale: `derive_ack_requirement()` currently depends only on `requires_ack` and `acknowledged_at` in `crates/atm-core/src/read/state.rs:95-103`. `task_id` does not influence ack semantics. Task-backed message cases may still stay in regression coverage if helpful, but they are not the reason this classifier must move.
5. `InboxMessage` did not move in this phase and should not be re-homed as part of this fix. If the backend still needs the shared schema type after the classifier split, it must import the canonical `atm_storage::schema::InboxMessage` path rather than the `atm-core` re-export.

Required sealed-trait design decision:
1. The moved `NudgeTemplateOverrideStore` contract must declare whether the new `atm-storage` home keeps compiler-enforced sealing. This plan chooses yes: add an `atm-storage` owned sealed module for this contract family so `atm-storage-rusqlite` implements an `atm-storage` sealed trait instead of `atm-core`'s.
2. That does create a temporary asymmetry with existing `atm-storage` traits that are currently unsealed. The plan accepts that asymmetry explicitly rather than silently weakening the moved contract. Do not drop sealing just to match older unsealed `atm-storage` traits.
3. If the project later standardizes sealing across more `atm-storage` contracts, that should be a separate follow-up. It is not a prerequisite for this coupling fix.

Move instructions by file:
1. Move the storage-neutral enum/row definitions currently in `crates/atm-core/src/boundary/mod.rs` (`BuiltInNudgeTemplateKind`, `TeamNudgeTemplateOverrideMode`, `TeamNudgeTemplateOverrideRow`) into an `atm-storage` contract module, but leave `from_post_send_event` behind as an `atm-core` helper or extension path because it depends on `PostSendHookEvent`.
2. Move the trait currently in `crates/atm-core/src/boundary/store.rs` (`NudgeTemplateOverrideStore`) into the same `atm-storage` contract surface, with its sealing seam owned there.
3. Update `crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/nudge_template_override_store.rs`, `crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/shared_db.rs`, and `crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/lib.rs` to implement and return the `atm-storage` contract, not the `atm-core` one.
4. Update `crates/atm-core/src/lib.rs` and `crates/atm-core/src/boundary/mod.rs` / `store.rs` so the boundary facade keeps re-exporting the moved contract/types during the cutover.
5. Update all core-side imports in `crates/atm-core/src/send/nudge_template.rs`, `crates/atm-core/src/send/hook.rs`, `crates/atm-core/src/team_admin.rs`, `crates/atm-core/src/service_runtime.rs`, and `crates/atm-core/src/doctor/mod.rs` so they use the moved shared contract or the retained core-local helper, as appropriate.
6. Update the extra downstream consumers that rely on the current `atm-core` boundary path:
   - `crates/atm-runtime/src/composition.rs`
   - `crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/lib.rs`
   - `crates/atm/src/commands/internal_nudge.rs` test module
7. After those imports are repointed, the compatibility re-export remains in place, the boundary record/ADR path is updated, and the mailbox-metadata helper no longer reaches into `atm-core`, delete the normal Cargo edge in `crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/Cargo.toml`.

Tests that must move or be updated with the contract move:
1. `crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/nudge_template_override_store.rs`
   - `sqlite_override_store_saves_and_loads_override_row`
   - `sqlite_override_store_returns_none_for_missing_row`
   - `sqlite_override_store_returns_none_after_override_row_is_deleted`
   - `sqlite_override_store_rejects_empty_override_body`
   - `sqlite_override_store_disables_and_clears_rows`
   - `sqlite_override_store_migrates_legacy_empty_rows_to_disabled`
2. `crates/atm-core/src/boundary/store.rs`
   - `nudge_template_override_store_trait_is_object_safe_and_compiles`
3. `crates/atm-core/src/send/nudge_template.rs`
   - `resolve_template_body_uses_default_when_no_override_exists`
   - `resolve_template_body_treats_disabled_override_as_disabled`
   - `resolve_template_uses_explicit_override_body`
   - `qualified_sender_identity_uses_sender_and_team`
   - `render_built_in_nudge_populates_placeholders`
4. `crates/atm-core/src/send/hook.rs`
   - `graft_fallback_dispatches_through_emitter_without_tmux_fields`
   - plus the `HookEmissionRuntime` fixture methods whose signatures currently expose the `atm-core` nudge override row/kind types.
5. `crates/atm-core/src/team_admin.rs`
   - `set_nudge_template_override_rejects_invalid_kind`
   - `set_nudge_template_override_rejects_empty_body`
   - `set_nudge_template_override_rejects_caller_team_mismatch`
   - `set_nudge_template_override_saves_row_through_boundary`
   - `disable_nudge_template_override_saves_disabled_row_through_boundary`
   - `clear_nudge_template_override_deletes_row_and_reports_state`
   - plus the `RecordingNudgeTemplateOverrideStore` test fixture.
6. `crates/atm-core/src/service_runtime.rs`
   - `rebuild_compat_inbox_projection_reexports_store_backed_mailbox`
   - plus the `NoopNudgeTemplateOverrideStore` fixture and `RetainedServiceRuntime::load_nudge_template_override` signatures.
7. `crates/atm-core/src/doctor/mod.rs`
   - doctor tests compile through `NoopNudgeTemplateOverrideStore`; that fixture must be repointed to the moved shared contract even though the individual doctor assertions are unchanged.
8. `crates/atm/src/commands/internal_nudge.rs`
   - `built_in_template_kind_selection_covers_six_paths`
   - plus any other test helpers in that module that currently call `BuiltInNudgeTemplateKind::from_post_send_event`; those callers must switch to the retained `atm-core` helper once the storage-neutral enum move happens.
9. `crates/atm-runtime/src/composition.rs`
   - compile coverage for `RuntimeAssembly.nudge_template_override_store`
   - `with_default_nudge_template_override_store`
   - plus any tests or debug fixtures that still spell the old `atm_core::boundary` contract type.
10. `crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/lib.rs`
   - compile coverage for `with_default_nudge_template_override_store`
   - this file remains production scope even if it does not carry its own dedicated unit tests today.

Tests that must be rewritten for the mailbox-metadata helper split:
1. `crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/lib.rs`
   - `query_mailbox_metadata_rejects_invalid_task_id`
2. `crates/atm-core/src/list.rs`
   - any coverage that asserts `pending_ack` list rendering derived from the classifier
3. `crates/atm-core/src/service_runtime_store.rs`
   - coverage around `shared_message_to_metadata_row`
4. `crates/atm-runtime/src/legacy_storage_adapters.rs`
   - coverage around `mailbox_row`
5. `crates/atm-core/src/read/state.rs`
   - classifier unit coverage remains the source of truth and should be updated only if the classifier itself moves to `atm-storage`
6. Add or update a direct metadata regression that proves the new shared classifier still computes `requires_ack` and `pending_ack` correctly for:
   - plain messages
   - `requires_ack` messages with no acknowledgement
   - acknowledged messages
   - optionally task-backed messages as ordinary fixtures only, not because task state changes the classifier

Closure condition:
The fix is not complete until:
- `atm-storage-rusqlite` has no production imports from `atm-core`
- `atm-storage-rusqlite` has no `atm_core::boundary::sealed::Sealed` implementation
- the canonical `NudgeTemplateOverrideStore` boundary record and its paired human-readable doc no longer claim `atm-core` ownership
- the required ADR-021 replacement/ruling for the ownership relocation is recorded
- `atm-core` compatibility re-exports exist for the moved types until `atm-runtime`, `atm-daemon-bootstrap`, and `atm` no longer rely on the old path
- the preferred shared ack-classifier move covers the real consumer set (`read/state.rs`, `list.rs`, `service_runtime_store.rs`, `legacy_storage_adapters.rs`, and `mailbox_metadata.rs`)
- only after those steps are complete is removing the normal `atm-storage-rusqlite -> atm-core` Cargo dependency an achievable and valid closure target
- the moved contract plus mailbox-metadata tests are green on the new shared contract path.""" .

